    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0249" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/pg202"/>

                <head>156. Letter from Clough to McConaughy<anchor n="1" xml:id="d156-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-09-01">September 1,
                        1955</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Walter:</salute>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d156-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d156-1"/>
                <p>I am enclosing copies of our draft agreed announcement and the Ambassador’s
                    statement explaining the changes in the draft, both of which were used at the
                    12th meeting with the Chinese Communists on August 31. These are the texts
                    promised you in telegram No. 661, August 31st, paragraph one.</p>
                <p>Alex is now in Prague and the rest of us are holding the fort here until his
                    return Sunday night.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Ralph N.
                            Clough</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <pb facs="0250" n="203" type="typeset" xml:id="pg203"/>



                <xi:include href="d156-a1.xml" xpointer="d156-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d156-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d156-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Geneva Talks Files, Lot 72D415. Confidential;
                    Official–Informal. Enclosure 1, “Draft Agreed Announcement,” is attached but not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
